    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0453" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/5–2446</note>
                <head>No. 260<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Briefing Book Paper</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d260-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russian Participation in European Economic
                        Organizations</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">recommendation</hi>
                </p>
                <p>It is recommended that we endeavor to obtain agreement from the Soviet Government
                    to participate fully in … the European Central Inland Transport Organization
                    (ECITO), … including designation of representatives to cooperate in the
                    day-to-day activities of these organizations.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">discussion</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>… Principally due to disagreement on the issue of Polish representation, the
                    Soviets have not participated in recent discussions concerning the ECITO. Their
                    delegation in London, however, has informally indicated that the present
                        agreement<anchor n="2" xml:id="d260-f2"/> has substantially met the
                    objections which they had to earlier drafts. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-03">July 3,
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="1" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>For the full text of this paper, see <ref target="#d525">document No. 525</ref>.
                    The recommendation here printed also appears in substantially the same language
                    in <ref target="#d524">document No. 524</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d260-f2" n="2" xml:id="d260-f2-content">
                <p>For the text of the agreement as signed on September 27, 1945, see Executive
                    Agreement Series No. 494; 59 Stat. (2) 1740.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
